{{also|mjölk|mjǫlk|mjølk}}
==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{der|fo|non|mjǫlk}}, {{m|non|mjolk}}, from {{der|fo|gem-pro|*meluks}}, cognate with {{cog|da|mælk}}, {{cog|sv|mjölk}}, {{cog|en|milk}}. Ultimately from {{der|fo|ine-pro|*h₂melǵ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|fo|[mjœl̥k]}}, ''[[Suðuroy]]:'' {{IPA|fo|[mjʏl̥k]}}

===Noun===
{{fo-noun|f|mjólkar|-}}

# [[milk]]

====Declension====
{{fo-decl-noun-f2-s|mjólk}}
Note the lack of i-mutation in the genitive (from *melukiz ). Although the form would suggest a mutated **''mýlkur'', ''-jó-'' is not the original vowel (from *-eu-, as in {{m|fo|tjóð}} ), but a product of a double vowel change, first fracture: meluk- > mjǫlk, and then lengthening: o/ǫ > ó before lk. Also, the ability of the -iz to effect an i-mutation on the first vowel is reduced by the intermediate -u-.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|fo|mjólkardropi}}
* {{l|fo|mjólkarsjokuláta}}
* {{l|fo|mjólkarsýra}}
* {{l|fo|kokusmjólk}}
* {{l|fo|knívur mátti ikki fara í mjólk - bert skeið ella spónur og krúss}} - a knife may never go in milk - only scoop, spoon and mug

===See also===
* {{l|fo|ostur}}
* {{l|fo|smør}}
* {{l|fo|kjøt}}
* {{l|fo|ull}}

